1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,132
Practice interviews ask you to rate yourself.

2
00:00:02,182 --> 00:00:04,072
But you can't rate what you never said.

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:05,490
This is sixty.

4
00:00:07,766 --> 00:00:11,641
sixty is a spoken interview coach for engineers moving into AI roles.

5
00:00:11,691 --> 00:00:15,338
You answer out loud, and it tells you exactly what you left out.

6
00:00:15,388 --> 00:00:19,036
The grade runs on NVIDIA Nemotron, through Nebius Token Factory.

7
00:00:19,608 --> 00:00:23,211
Here is a real interview question: design a production RAG system.

8
00:00:23,261 --> 00:00:26,698
In the app you speak, and the transcript fills in as you talk.

9
00:00:26,748 --> 00:00:30,019
To show you, I'll let a synthetic voice play the candidate.

10
00:01:02,486 --> 00:01:05,870
You can fix any mis-heard words before anything is graded.

11
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,173
Then, rate my answer.

12
00:01:07,437 --> 00:01:08,928
Now the part that matters.

13
00:01:08,978 --> 00:01:12,188
Nemotron Nano first splits the answer into its points.

14
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:17,108
Then Nano and Ultra each rate every point, independently, on Nebius Token Factory.

15
00:01:17,158 --> 00:01:19,657
Every finding must quote your exact words.

16
00:01:19,707 --> 00:01:21,969
A quote you never said is thrown away.

17
00:01:27,366 --> 00:01:28,389
Here is the result.

18
00:01:28,439 --> 00:01:29,858
Two scores, side by side.

19
00:01:29,908 --> 00:01:34,039
Where the models split, you see both views, and nothing is averaged away.

20
00:01:34,089 --> 00:01:38,107
Every sentence you said is colour coded by how the two models rated it.

21
00:01:38,157 --> 00:01:41,271
And at the top, one line to act on: say this next time.

22
00:01:41,837 --> 00:01:43,394
Don't take the grade on trust.

23
00:01:43,444 --> 00:01:51,644
Open the proof, and you can see where the models agree, point by point, and exactly which calls ran: the models, the time each took, and the tokens used.

24
00:01:54,419 --> 00:01:56,365
Then the coach doesn't stop at a score.

25
00:01:56,415 --> 00:02:03,529
It asks a different question that tests the same idea, so a gap only closes when you cover it on a question you haven't just seen answered.

26
00:02:04,013 --> 00:02:08,545
Your recording never leaves your browser, and your progress stays on your device.

27
00:02:08,595 --> 00:02:11,939
sixty runs on NVIDIA Nemotron through Nebius Token Factory.

28
00:02:11,989 --> 00:02:14,598
Try it at nvidia hackethon dot vercel dot app.

